SEALING PROCEDURE - THE GEDO STATUE
CORE ORGANISATION TECHNIQUE. All ten ring-bearers required.

The Gedo Statue is the vessel into which every tailed beast is sealed. It is summoned
by the Leader through the Rinnegan and stands at the heart of the sealing chamber.

Procedure:
1. The Leader summons the Gedo Statue. Its mouth opens; nine sealed eyes wait on its
   brow, one per beast already taken.
2. All ten ring-bearers take their assigned positions atop the Statue's fingers, in
   person or by chakra projection. Each ring corresponds to a fixed finger.
3. The bearers form the Illusionary Dragon Nine Consuming Seals technique. Spectral
   dragons issue from the Statue's mouth and seize the beast's chakra from the host.
4. The beast is drawn out of the jinchuriki and into the Statue over three days and
   three nights. On completion the host dies and a new eye opens on the Statue.

The Statue must not be interrupted mid-seal. A broken extraction risks the beast, the
bearers, and the chamber. Guard the site absolutely until the eye opens.
